# A field whose type is a union of string literals holds a small number for each literal. The switch loads the field once and compares that word with one constant per case: no string is read.
# The switch names every literal, so what is neither of the first two is the third.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="areaOf" role=Source
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[kind]] = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isCircle]] = Equal(b@[[kind]], $18(
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[isCircle]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[isSquare]] = Equal(b@[[kind]], $22(
# CHECK: Branch(b@[[isSquare]], Terminal)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-NOT: Equal(b@[[kind]]
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[shape]], offset = 32, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Inside a case the fields of that member of the union are read without a test of the shape.
# NONE-LABEL: name="areaOf" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: Reads:StringImpl
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSRopeString
# NONE-NOT: Reads:ShapeWords
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
